# tasks_heap_success: HeapTextureSizeAndAlign (64) answered: the reply, {u64 size, u64 align}, is written at the reply offset. The test's own Metal query is recorded beside it, with allowGPUOptimizedContents at Metal's default (YES); the guest's descriptor clears that bit, and the two differ (section 6.10). A reply of 16 bytes and one of 0x3fff straddling two pages; a longer payload than the descriptor needs. Over a read-only page the reply is refused where the task maps with writability (map: "Failed to make mapping"; the service), and written anyway in the blocks setup, whose mapping ignores it. Below version 43 the command is unsupported.
